Honour SystemChrome.setPreferredOrientations (needs 0007).

The platform plugin passes the allowed orientations, most preferred first, to
the window. When Lipstick reports a rotation to an orientation the app doesn't
allow, the content stays where it is; if the current orientation becomes
disallowed, it moves to the most preferred one. The Qt surface extension's
content orientation mask is updated to match. An empty list allows any.

Mapping (portrait panel): portraitUp = 0, landscapeLeft = 270,
portraitDown = 180, landscapeRight = 90 (wl_output transforms).
A landscape-only app keeps its landscape content while shown as a cover.

